# Local credential scratch files.
#
# `/auth` holds a GitHub personal access token in plain text. It is ignored so
# it can never be swept up by `git add -A` — a token in a public repo is
# scraped and used within minutes of being pushed.
#
# THE LEADING SLASH IS ESSENTIAL. Written as bare `auth`, the pattern matches
# every path segment of that name at any depth, which silently excluded
# `src/lib/auth/`, `src/app/api/auth/` and `src/components/auth/` — the entire
# authentication system — from the commit. The slash anchors it to the repo
# root, where the credential file actually is.
/auth
/auth.txt
*.token

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

